msgid "Qute templates"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We are very pleased to announce the 1.11.0 release of Quarkus Tools for "
"IntelliJ.\n"
"This release adds support for Qute templates but also align with LSP4MP 0.4."
"0 and quarkus-ls 0.11.1."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When a Quarkus project has Qute in the classpath, editing a Qute template "
"(HTML / JSON / YAML / Text) will add new features into the editor."
msgstr ""

msgid "Let's do a little tour."
msgstr ""

msgid "Integration between Qute templates and Java"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Now any `Template` attribute will show the option to generate a "
"corresponding Qute template, or navigate to the existing template file."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All Qute files paired with a corresponding Java resource support a number of "
"language client features, such as go to definition, hover, autocompletion, "
"etc.. Each of these we will explore further in the article"
msgstr ""

msgid "Method Parameter Support in Qute Templates"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Qute language server has support for built-in and user-defined Java "
"classes, including parameter completion and validation for their methods. "
"Take advantage of this to easily avoid Java related mistakes."
msgstr ""

msgid "Java Type Hover Support for Qute Templates"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Alongside support for Java completion and validation, the extension also "
"supports type hovering for built-in and user-defined Java classes."
msgstr ""

msgid "Qute Section Completion"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Qute templates use sections in its templating language to power any logic "
"required when compiling and displaying the resulting document. To support "
"this, the extension’s Qute support populates a completion list with all "
"available Qute sections, along with any parameters they take and a small "
"code snippet of their usage."
msgstr ""

msgid "Support for Qute Validation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Java and Qute validation is included for Qute templates with Quarkus Tools "
"for IntelliJ, including diagnostics."
msgstr ""

msgid "Completion for Qute Value Resolvers"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Paired with corresponding Java methods, built-in Java classes also have "
"built-in Qute value resolvers made available by the Qute templating engine "
"that are evaluated and output, or resolve to, a value. Quarkus Tools for "
"IntelliJ supports completion, hover and snippet generation for these built-"
"in value resolvers."
msgstr ""

msgid "Support for @TemplateExtension Methods"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Template extension methods are used to extend the set of accessible "
"properties of data objects. Qute support in Quarkus Tools for IntelliJ has "
"support for marked `@TemplateExtension` Java methods, which extend a given "
"data model."
msgstr ""

msgid "Support for Directly Injecting Beans into Qute Templates"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A CDI bean annotated with `@Named` can be referenced in any template through "
"cdi and/or inject namespaces. Quarkus Tools for IntelliJ provides completion "
"and definition navigation support for Beans."
msgstr ""

msgid "Improved features"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In addition to the new Qute support, we've enhanced existing features around "
"MicroProfile 2.0 and Quarkus 2.x new features."
msgstr ""

msgid "Configs all the way down"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"While we had support for configuration profiles through property prefixing "
"(eg. `%dev.name`), we now also support profile-aware files. We’ve added "
"support for this, and many other features part of the MicroProfile 2.0 "
"release."
msgstr ""

msgid "MicroProfile Fault Tolerance"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We’ve added basic validation support for `@Bulkhead`, `@Timeout`, "
"`@Asynchronous`, and `@Scheduled` annotations."
msgstr ""

msgid "Application Path support"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When launching a Quarkus application, the code lens URL endpoints now "
"supports `@ApplicationPath` and will take its value into account."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In this example, the `@ApplicationPath` is set to `/api`, and the code on "
"the method declaration (below) takes that into account when generating the "
"URL."
msgstr ""

msgid "Completions"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"At the end of the day, everyone wants to spend less time trying to hunt down "
"some obscure setting, and more time developing the logic."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you’re using the `@CacheResult` annotation on a method in your Java "
"sources, we automatically suggest the settings available to configure it "
"from your configuration file. It’s also fairly reactive to changes so you’ll "
"always know if something has gone wrong."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`@ConfigMapping` is now also supported with some basic validation as well as "
"completion for the application properties."
msgstr ""

msgid "Moving Forward"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you have any questions,\n"
"suggestions or feedback, by all means please https://github.com/redhat-"
"developer/intellij-quarkus/issues[open an issue]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Thank you for reading and stay tuned for the next release!"
msgstr ""

msgid "Links"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"GitHub repository: https://github.com/redhat-developer/intellij-quarkus"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Open an issue: https://github.com/redhat-developer/intellij-quarkus/issues"
msgstr ""
